{"segments": [{"start": 0.0, "end": 2.62, "text": "while people do not prioritize spending"}, {"start": 2.62, "end": 3.96, "text": "on the things they love."}, {"start": 4.1, "end": 5.38, "text": "That's not the way people act."}, {"start": 5.7, "end": 7.36, "text": "And this is one of the central mistakes"}, {"start": 7.36, "end": 9.54, "text": "that the entire financial industry makes,"}, {"start": 9.68, "end": 12.92, "text": "which is to treat people like they are rational robots."}, {"start": 13.64, "end": 17.0, "text": "Oh, people, they believe that their children"}, {"start": 17.0, "end": 18.48, "text": "are the most important thing to them."}, {"start": 18.56, "end": 21.42, "text": "So therefore they are apportioning resources accordingly."}, {"start": 21.66, "end": 22.26, "text": "No, they're not."}, {"start": 22.66, "end": 24.12, "text": "They're not doing that at all."}, {"start": 24.44, "end": 25.34, "text": "And so when I asked them,"}, {"start": 25.42, "end": 26.52, "text": "what's the most important thing to you?"}, {"start": 26.56, "end": 27.48, "text": "The answers are always the same."}, {"start": 27.48, "end": 30.02, "text": "The number one thing that people love to spend money on"}, {"start": 30.02, "end": 32.2, "text": "is food, eating out, fine."}, {"start": 32.88, "end": 34.24, "text": "Number two is travel."}, {"start": 34.52, "end": 35.54, "text": "Number three is health and wellness."}, {"start": 35.98, "end": 38.3, "text": "Then we take a look at where their money is actually going."}, {"start": 39.14, "end": 41.44, "text": "It is never aligned, never."}, {"start": 41.92, "end": 43.96, "text": "And so what they claim is important to them"}, {"start": 43.96, "end": 46.28, "text": "is not reflected on their calendar"}, {"start": 46.76, "end": 47.9, "text": "and in their spending plan."}], "words": [{"w": "while", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.04}, {"w": "people", "start": 0.04, "end": 0.24}, {"w": "do", "start": 0.24, "end": 0.52}, {"w": "not", "sta